.TH CVECTOR_FIND 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_find \- find the index of the first occurrence of an element
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

size_t cvector_find(cvec v, const void *elem,
                    ccol_comparison_proc_t cmp);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Does a linear scan and returns the zero-based index of the first element
that is equal to *elem. When cmp is NULL, the function compares with
memcmp over the element size, which is equality byte by byte.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v     Vector to search (must not be NULL)
elem  Pointer to the value to search for
cmp   Comparison function (int(*)(const void*,const void*)), or NULL
      to use memcmp
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Zero-based index of the first element that matches.
ccol_invalid_size when there is no match, and when elem is NULL.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(n) complexity
Asserts if v is NULL
Structs with padding bytes may not compare correctly when cmp is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_find (3)
